# Git commits — explicit only

**CRITICAL:** Create a git commit **only** when the user explicitly asks to commit (e.g. “commit”, “commit this”, “make a commit”).

- Do **not** commit because work “looks done”, a feature shipped, tests passed, or you are “going with the flow”.
- Do **not** invent a commit as a default wrap-up step.
- If commit intent is unclear, ask first — do not assume.
- Staging, committing, and pushing are separate: only do what the user named.
